node_modules
dist

# NOT committed, on purpose — app-vite does the same.
#
# This lockfile gets regenerated on Windows every time `npm install` runs on the
# laptop, and a Windows-resolved lockfile omits the linux-x64 builds of the
# native binaries rollup and @tailwindcss/oxide ship as optional platform
# packages. The Docker image then installs cold without them and `vite build`
# dies with "Cannot find module @rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu".
#
# The Dockerfile deletes it defensively too, so a stray committed copy cannot
# break a deploy. If one is already tracked: git rm --cached cbedge-v3/package-lock.json
package-lock.json
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
.vite
generated/
